    "text": "**Phil Larkin – Professional Clown**\n\n---\n\n**Section 1: Professional Summary**\n\nPhil Larkin is a dynamic and engaging professional clown with over 10 years of experience in the circus and entertainment industry. Known for his ability to entertain, connect with audiences, and bring joy to any performance, Phil combines humor, creativity, and a deep sense of humor to create unforgettable experiences. He is a versatile performer who excels in acrobatics, clowning, and storytelling, and is passionate about using performance as a tool for emotional expression and community engagement.\n\n---\n\n**Section 2: Professional Experience**\n\n**Professional Clown / Circus Performer**  \n*The Larkin Circus*  \n*New York, NY | 2015–Present*\n\n- Performs in both live and digital entertainment, including circus, comedy, and interactive performances.\n- Creates and executes original acts that blend humor, storytelling, and physical comedy.\n- Works with a diverse audience, from children to adults, to ensure inclusive and engaging experiences.\n- Collaborates with directors, choreographers, and other performers to develop innovative and entertaining shows.\n\n**Circus Trainer / Clown Instructor**  \n*Clowning Academy of New York*  \n*New York, NY | 2012–2015*\n\n- Trains and mentors aspiring clowns and performers in the art of clowning and performance.\n- Develops and teaches workshops on clowning techniques, storytelling, and audience interaction.\n- Provides feedback and support to students, helping them grow both professionally and personally.\n\n**Section 3: Education & Certifications**\n\n**Bachelor of Arts in Performing Arts**  \n*University of New York, New York City*  \n*2010–2014*\n\n- Major in Theater and Performance Studies.\n- Skilled in acting, stagecraft, and performance psychology.\n- Graduated with honors.\n\n**Certification in Clowning and Performance Psychology**  \n*Clowning Institute of America*  \n*2016*\n\n- Advanced training in clowning techniques, emotional expression, and audience engagement.\n- Certified in the use of clowning as a therapeutic tool.\n\n**Section 4: Skills & Qualifications**\n\n**Skills:**\n\n- Performances in a variety of circus and comedy acts.\n- Skilled in acrobatics, juggling, and physical comedy.\n- Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n- Ability to adapt to different audience sizes and environments.\n- Proficient in both live and digital performance platforms.\n\n**Qualifications:**\n\n- 1",
